    "body": "Problem:\r\ncommit_chars_str() reads a 0x80-0xBF byte as a 2-byte lead, so \"\\xA9x\" makes \"x\" a commit character. nvim_get_hl() returns a dict, so `#` on it is 0 whether or not the group exists\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\nuse vim.str_utf_end() and drop entries that are not one whole character. use next check dict length.\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-28T12:39:04Z",
